      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(-4,6)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which point must lie on $y=-f(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The transformation $y=-f(x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(-4,6)$ lies $6$ units *above* the $x$-axis. So, under the action of the transformation, this point will be reflected $6$ units *below* the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273614/assets/5f31409152fd448245c945e32064a37779427a087657cff485e3001858be27bf.png)\n\nWe conclude that the point $(-4,-6)$ must lie on the graph of $y=-f(x).$",
